# What the guardians and the Grimoire say during a battle, when the Hint Director decides someone
# should speak (data/hints.json says when). One node per hint, one line per node.
# Node names: <guardian>_<topic> for a guardian's taunt (it contains a real hint, in character),
# grimoire_<topic>_<step> for the Grimoire (nudge, shape, offer: each more explicit).
# Placeholders: {mode} is the guardian's current mode, read from its brain's explain(), so a
# taunt never lies about what the guardian is doing. Item and spell names stay in English.
# Draft lines (prompt 03); the real writing is prompt 07, by humans. See docs/WRITING.md.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the Asterisk Slime

== slime_world ==
Asterisk Slime: You broke my table, little witch. Do you know how to {wave}put it back{/wave}?

== slime_heal ==
Asterisk Slime: Low on HP, and a Healing Herb still sitting in your items? Splendid. I am {mode}, and hungry.

== slime_ether ==
Asterisk Slime: No mana left? Your satchel holds an Ether, and you have never once read it.

== slime_overflow ==
Asterisk Slime: {shake}Splat!{/shake} Half your spells fell off the page again. Even a slime knows when to stop.

== slime_habit ==
Asterisk Slime: The same query, a third time. I am {mode}, not stupid: I know it by heart now.

== slime_enemies ==
Asterisk Slime: You keep casting, but you have never looked at me. I am in a table too, you know.

== slime_items ==
Asterisk Slime: Witches carry things. Do you even know what is in your items?

== slime_stuck ==
Asterisk Slime: Blub? Is the witch asleep again? I can wait. I am {mode}. I am a slime.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Sir Wherewell

== knight_world ==
Sir Wherewell: You damaged the records of this keep. Only a fool fights on a broken floor. Can you put it back?

== knight_heal ==
Sir Wherewell: You are wounded, and you carry a Healing Herb you have never used. I am {mode}: I will not wait for you.

== knight_ether ==
Sir Wherewell: Your mana is spent. There is an Ether in your items. In your place, I would read it.

== knight_overflow ==
Sir Wherewell: Twice now your spells spilled past the page. Ask for fewer rows, or ask for {color gold}better{/color} ones.

== knight_habit ==
Sir Wherewell: The same spell for the third time. I am {mode}, and my ward has learned its shape.

== knight_enemies ==
Sir Wherewell: You strike without knowing me. My weakness is written in the enemies table, for anyone who reads.

== knight_items ==
Sir Wherewell: A witch who never opens her items fights with one hand.

== knight_stuck ==
Sir Wherewell: I am {mode}, and still you hesitate. Write something, witch.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the Grimoire

== grimoire_world_nudge ==
Grimoire: The world changed under us. F6 opens the rewind page: we can go back to before it broke.

== grimoire_heal_shape ==
Grimoire: Your HP is low. Read the herb from your items: {rune SELECT} name FROM items {rune WHERE} name = 'Healing Herb'.

== grimoire_ether_shape ==
Grimoire: Out of mana? {rune SELECT} name FROM items {rune WHERE} name = 'Ether' drinks one.

== grimoire_overflow_nudge ==
Grimoire: Only four rows fit on my right page. The rest are paid for, and lost.

== grimoire_overflow_shape ==
Grimoire: End your query with {rune LIMIT}, like this: SELECT name FROM spells LIMIT 4.

== grimoire_habit_nudge ==
Grimoire: The same spell again and again. Guardians learn. Try another element, or another filter.

== grimoire_enemies_nudge ==
Grimoire: Who are we fighting, witch? The enemies table knows.

== grimoire_enemies_shape ==
Grimoire: Look before you strike: {rune SELECT} * FROM enemies. Read its weakness column.

== grimoire_enemies_offer ==
Grimoire: Press F3 and I will show you the exact query, and how to read what it returns.

== grimoire_items_nudge ==
Grimoire: You carry things, witch. They live in the items table, and every name you read from it is used.

== grimoire_items_shape ==
Grimoire: Pick one item by name: {rune SELECT} name FROM items {rune WHERE} name = 'Healing Herb'. Reading every row uses every item.

== grimoire_stuck_offer ==
Grimoire: Stuck? Press F3, and I will write the next query with you.
